self — The receiver parameter for instance methods.

Syntax:
  interface Greeter {
    function greet(self) -> string
  }
  
  class Person {
    name: string
    implements Greeter {
      function greet(self) -> string {
        return self.name
      }
    }
  }

`self` is the value receiver in class and interface methods. Use capital `Self` only in type positions, such as `Self.Item` for an associated type projection.
